---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { links } from "../data/site";
import { withBase } from "../lib/paths";

const version = "1.0";
const updated = "30 October 2026";
---

<Base
  title="Terms"
  description="What Pesa Clarity does, your part, and the law that applies."
>
  <article class="container terms-page">
    <div class="prose">
      <p class="eyebrow">Terms</p>
      <h1>Terms</h1>
      <p class="muted">
        Version {version}, updated {updated}.
      </p>

      <h2>The short version</h2>
      <p>
        Pesa Clarity is a free app that turns your M-Pesa and bank messages into
        a simple daily budget. It helps you plan; the decisions stay yours. By
        using the app you agree to these terms and to our{" "}
        <a href={withBase("/privacy/")}>privacy policy</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>Who can use it</h2>
      <p>
        Pesa Clarity is for people aged 18 and over, using their own phone and
        their own accounts.
      </p>

      <h2>What the app does</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          It reads messages and statements from the accounts you choose, on your
          phone.
        </li>
        <li>
          It suggests categories, budgets and a safe-to-spend figure from what
          it reads.
        </li>
        <li>Messages it is still learning wait for you to check.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Pesa Clarity is a budgeting tool. It is not a bank or a lender, and it
        never moves money. Its figures are estimates to help you plan, not
        financial advice. Check anything important against your statements.
      </p>

      <h2>Your part</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          Keep your phone, PIN and vault passphrase safe. Only you know the
          passphrase, so keep a copy somewhere secure.
        </li>
        <li>
          Correct anything the app reads wrongly, so your budget stays right.
        </li>
        <li>Use the app and our server only as they are meant to be used.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Your account</h2>
      <p>
        An account is only used for sign-in and backups, and you can use the app
        without one. You can delete your account from inside the app at any
        time. We may pause an account that is used to attack or overload our
        server.
      </p>

      <h2>Open source</h2>
      <p>
        The app's code is open source under the GNU Affero General Public
        License 3.0, and the message parsers under the Apache License 2.0. You
        can read, build and change it under those licences. These terms cover
        the app and the server we run.
      </p>

      <h2>Changes</h2>
      <p>
        We keep improving Pesa Clarity, so features may change. When these terms
        change, the version and date at the top change too, and the release
        notes say what is new.
      </p>

      <h2>Our responsibility</h2>
      <p>
        We work hard to keep Pesa Clarity accurate and available, and we provide
        it as it is. As far as Kenyan law allows, we are not responsible for
        losses from decisions made using the app. Nothing in these terms limits
        your rights under the Consumer Protection Act 2012 or the Data
        Protection Act 2019.
      </p>

      <h2>Kenyan law</h2>
      <p>
        These terms are governed by the laws of Kenya, and Kenyan courts hear
        any dispute about them.
      </p>

      <h2>Questions</h2>
      <p>
        Ask in public on GitHub (
        <a href={links.github}>github.com/pesaclarity</a>).
      </p>
    </div>
  </article>
</Base>

<style>
  .terms-page {
    padding-block: var(--space-7) var(--space-8);
  }

  h2 {
    margin-top: var(--space-6);
  }
</style>
